<Base title="FAQ" description="Repo, GitHub, privacy, depth, and the knowledge-graph question — answered plainly.">
  <h1>FAQ</h1>
  <p class="lede">Short, plain answers to the questions people actually ask.</p>

  <h3>Do I need to know how to code, or use GitHub?</h3>
  <p>No. Open the spec gist in Zo Computer, or copy the raw Markdown into a new folder, and ask Zo to read <code>spec.md</code>. That’s the setup.</p>

  <h3>What do I actually download?</h3>
  <p>One small folder. The file that matters is <code>spec.md</code> — the instructions Zo follows to interview you and build your brain.</p>

  <h3>Is this a template I have to fill in?</h3>
  <p>No. There are no blank pages or fake examples to clean up. Zo creates files <em>after</em> it learns your real context and you approve the plan.</p>

  <h3>Will it dump a giant structure on me?</h3>
  <p>Only if you ask for it. You pick a depth — Starter is four files. Zo never writes anything until you say yes.</p>

  <h3>Does it use fake example projects or sample clients?</h3>
  <p>No. Your brain starts from your actual projects, people, sources, and decisions — nothing prefilled.</p>

  <h3>Can I start small and grow?</h3>
  <p>Yes. Begin at Starter and move up to Beginner, Intermediate, or Pro whenever you need more. The brain is meant to compound over time.</p>

  <h3>Where does my information live? Is it private?</h3>
  <p>It’s plain Markdown files in your own Zo workspace. You own them. No database required.</p>

  <h3>What’s the “knowledge graph” / Vivary thing?</h3>
  <p>That’s Pro depth only, and entirely optional. At Pro, your brain can behave like a personal knowledge graph — typed entities, relationships, provenance, and routed reads — while still being ordinary Markdown. Most people never need it, and that’s fine.</p>

  <h3>Do I have to use Zo Computer?</h3>
  <p>The system is built for Zo — <code>spec.md</code> is written as Zo’s setup prompt, and Zo does the interviewing and building. That’s where it shines.</p>

  <h2>Ready to start?</h2>
  <CtaButtons note="Open the gist, then ask Zo: “Read spec.md and help me set up my Minimal Zo Brain.”" />
</Base>
